<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Fingerhut downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Fingerhut downgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>- Dain Bosworth lowered its rating and cut earnings estimates for Fingerhut Companies Inc after the direct marketer increased its bad debt provision.</p>
<p>- Dain Bosworth analyst Dean Ramos said he lowered his rating to hold from buy due to a reduction in earnings estimates and a decline in confidence in credit managment going forward.</p>
<p>- Ramos trimmed his earnings estimate for Fingerhut's fourth quarter to $0.86 a share from $1.06, its fiscal 1996 year to $1.04 from $1.24 and its fiscal 1997 year to $1.35 from $1.50.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
